        "texto": "Etsadah, “bracelet,” is, according to Gesenius, more properly an anklet than a bracelet; yet as it is here spoken of in connection with the arm it doubtless means an armlet. The word occurs also in Numbers 31:50 where it is associated with tsamid, (bracelet,) and is rendered “cha…"
